      "side": 1,
      "message": "lib.rs.h includes only the Rust parts of this file - so it gets KeyResult and the things it needs, but not this include!.\n\nThe include! actually feeds into a different header - rust/cxx.h - which I\u0027m not including or indeed generating any more (it\u0027s redundant here).\n\nMore importantly it is injected into the generated C++ source code (composd_native_cxx_generated.cc) which exposes the real ffi function to Rust and calls my implementation - there it\u0027s necessary so it can see my prototype.\n\nThere is some redundancy, but the generated code use #if guards to make sure we don\u0027t end up with duplicate definitions. And no circularity.",
